00:45:31.312 --> 00:45:34.681
somebody that's just like you that
got into Stanford at some point.

00:45:34.681 --> 00:45:40.864
And so you have, like you will have
a shot to get in as much as anybody does.

00:45:40.864 --> 00:45:45.400
So, yeah,
that's what I would say about that.

00:45:45.400 --> 00:45:51.022
&gt;&gt; Thanks, Parker, and thank you
Amanda for weighing in on chat there.

00:45:51.022 --> 00:45:55.630
Natalia, Eric, anything come to mind for
either of you today?

00:45:55.630 --> 00:46:00.349
&gt;&gt; This is more advice for, I guess,
as you think about your class and

00:46:00.349 --> 00:46:03.383
your class is a big part
of your identity but

00:46:03.383 --> 00:46:08.865
both the partner in the student should
think about there's so many events and

00:46:08.865 --> 00:46:14.131
opportunities to interact with the class
above you and below you as well.

00:46:14.131 --> 00:46:18.373
I think that's sometimes
an opportunity that can be missed.

00:46:18.373 --> 00:46:23.486
And so if you and your partner kind
of plan to make sure that you don't

00:46:23.486 --> 00:46:29.258
just invest in the class that you're
a part of, but also the other classes.

00:46:29.258 --> 00:46:32.899
There's a lot of great like cross
pollination that can happen there,

00:46:32.899 --> 00:46:37.231
whether it's through social events or
even things like the women's golf clinic.

00:46:37.231 --> 00:46:40.782
There's all of these opportunities.

00:46:40.782 --> 00:46:44.340
&gt;&gt; Great advice.

00:46:44.340 --> 00:46:45.110
All right,

00:46:45.110 --> 00:46:50.117
we'd love to hear from the partners
thinking about the partner experience.

00:46:50.117 --> 00:46:55.226
Anything you did or in hindsight
wished you could have done in terms of

00:46:55.226 --> 00:47:00.440
supporting your students as they
were embarking on this experience.

00:47:00.440 --> 00:47:07.617
Or to the partners out there anything
you want to give them a heads up on?

00:47:07.617 --> 00:47:12.756
&gt;&gt; Yeah, I'll just I'll throw one
out there which is be flexible,

00:47:12.756 --> 00:47:16.413
be adaptable and
be willing to ask questions.

00:47:16.413 --> 00:47:21.322
I think as it as a partner
the especially fall quarter when there

00:47:21.322 --> 00:47:26.047
is just an inundation a day lusion
of new things that are going

00:47:26.047 --> 00:47:28.657
on that it's really important.

00:47:28.657 --> 00:47:32.689
I think to establish expectations,
establish routines and

00:47:32.689 --> 00:47:37.273
also recognize that the GSB can be
a really quirky place and sometimes

00:47:37.273 --> 00:47:42.109
you might be like why is my partner
prioritizing they're not over this.

00:47:42.109 --> 00:47:44.442
And I think it's just
kind of leaning into and

00:47:44.442 --> 00:47:47.770
being slightly flexible as
this experience really is.

00:47:47.770 --> 00:47:52.223
Transformational in so many different
ways and both for a partner and for

00:47:52.223 --> 00:47:53.829
the student themselves.

00:47:53.829 --> 00:47:58.176
And so yeah, I think being adaptable and
flexible and

00:47:58.176 --> 00:48:04.271
to ever said it earlier setting
expectations in the US is really critical.

00:48:04.271 --> 00:48:05.092
&gt;&gt; And, I agree with that.

00:48:05.092 --> 00:48:10.327
I also agree with what Amanda said
in the chat about working together.

00:48:10.327 --> 00:48:14.314
[LAUGH] And from the beginning, would have
been included whole of admissions process.

00:48:14.314 --> 00:48:17.738
And everybody's going to
have their own experience,

00:48:17.738 --> 00:48:21.562
but for us I will always talk
about the GSB like it was ours.

00:48:21.562 --> 00:48:25.702
Even though I didn't get a graduate
degree from the Stanford Graduate School

00:48:25.702 --> 00:48:26.472
of Business.

00:48:26.472 --> 00:48:31.009
Because I changed my life just
as much as I changed his and

00:48:31.009 --> 00:48:35.659
it disrupted and interrupted and
it transformed us too.

00:48:35.659 --> 00:48:38.785
And so for me,
it was important that I was involved.

00:48:38.785 --> 00:48:43.503
Every step of the way I read, every essay,
I read every application, and

00:48:43.503 --> 00:48:46.484
I celebrated the same way
when he got his call.

00:48:46.484 --> 00:48:53.215
And, so I think that that was something
that made it important for us.

00:48:53.215 --> 00:49:01.199
Is that we were in it together from
the very beginning until the end.

00:49:01.199 --> 00:49:02.064
&gt;&gt; Thank you Lacey Tory.

00:49:02.064 --> 00:49:06.323
&gt;&gt; I'll definitely echo that
the only thing I would add is

00:49:06.323 --> 00:49:09.110
depending on sort of where you are.

00:49:09.110 --> 00:49:15.643
Whether you're on campus or whether you're
